  {
   "type": "techDeepDive",
   "kicker": "Deep dive",
   "title": "How the outbox pattern adds replay to RabbitMQ",
   "subtitle": "One transaction, two writes, a relay that publishes",
   "concept": {
    "title": "Mechanism",
    "text": "The order service writes the order and an event row in **one database transaction**. A relay worker reads unsent rows in order and publishes them to the broker, then marks them sent.",
    "bullets": [
     "No dual-write: the event exists only if the order commits",
     "At-least-once delivery; consumers must be idempotent",
     "Replay = reset sent_at and let the relay re-publish",
     "Relay lag is the one metric to alert on"
    ]
   },
